WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.217 --> 00:00:04.160
- Every movie about
alcohol is normally so sad.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.030
- Yeah.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.630
- No one ever shows the upsides.

00:00:08.777 --> 00:00:11.500
(dynamic upbeat music)

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.040
- Hi, I'm Robert Eggers.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.306
- And I'm Robert Pattinson.

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:17.107
- And this is our "Scene Breakdown" for.

00:00:17.107 --> 00:00:19.225
- "The Lighthouse."

00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:22.392
(eerie melodic music)

00:00:24.063 --> 00:00:26.348
I think it was just water, but
we were drinking it though,

00:00:26.348 --> 00:00:29.290
I mean, there was, it was actually,

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:31.480
when I was talking about
this the other day,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.160
it's hard to do that.
- Yeah.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:35.810
- You literally can't, you
felt disgusting afterwards

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.367
and then it's kind of--

00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:40.380
- And we did like four takes of that.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.217
- Yeah, yeah, it's
really, really difficult

00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:43.170
to swallow like Willem,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.623
I've got a very pronounced gag reflex.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.693
- Yeah, and you guys, yeah.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:54.636
(eerie melodic music)

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.052
♪ Gypsy little whore, hoo rah ♪

00:00:58.052 --> 00:01:00.126
♪ I'm done with her, don't let me down ♪

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:03.593
- I mean, there was like
a very specific dance

00:01:03.593 --> 00:01:05.630
that we were supposed to be doing,

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.590
which you can sort of see Willem doing.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:10.570
Do you know, I guess I had a
different dance to rehearse,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.620
I had a kind of a lumberjack dance.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.360
- Yeah, but I mean,
you're doing all the moves

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.804
around the table with
Willem and everything.

00:01:16.804 --> 00:01:17.750
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:22.307
I feel like because my
character is so contained,

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.770
constricted and kind of
early in his sobriety,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:30.493
I kind of wanted to, it
wasn't just when he got drunk,

00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:32.752
'cause Willem was drinking the whole time,

00:01:32.752 --> 00:01:35.489
it wasn't like they would
end up on the same level.

00:01:35.489 --> 00:01:36.610
- [Robert E] Yeah, yeah, right.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.200
- They would just go way beyond,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.533
it's not like it's fun
to hang out with him,

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:43.430
- Yeah.
- literally it's like,

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:46.560
and then when he gets sort
of tender with him later,

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.385
when he's kind of tired and drunk,

00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:49.735
then it's even more there

00:01:49.735 --> 00:01:54.573
and it's like they could never
quite get on the same page,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.480
but I think that's kind
of what I was doing.

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.250
- Yeah, that makes total sense, yeah

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:06.400
and because generally things
are so tamped down in here,

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.353
the dancing and the drinking

00:02:07.353 --> 00:02:10.589
is just like revving you up to 110.

00:02:10.589 --> 00:02:14.672
(eerie melodic orchestral music)

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.593
- And he's been looking

00:02:24.593 --> 00:02:26.577
for Willem's validation the whole movie

00:02:26.577 --> 00:02:29.840
and it's kind of as soon as
he's getting his attention

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.830
and focus, it's literally like

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.310
he's been wanting a pat
on the head for so long,

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.485
that as soon as he gets
the attention on him,

00:02:36.485 --> 00:02:38.293
it's like a hyperactive child,

00:02:39.545 --> 00:02:42.860
like you just completely lose your mind.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:45.830
- Yeah, yeah and you're definitely trying

00:02:47.857 --> 00:02:51.425
to outdo his jig with
your lumberjack dance.

00:02:51.425 --> 00:02:53.270
By the way, you can't see Rob's feet,

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:57.130
but the dance he's doing
is incredibly complicated,

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.621
Robert Flatley would be very envious.

00:02:59.621 --> 00:03:01.160
- I think that's the only time

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:04.243
I've actually successfully
managed to do a spin,

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.110
like wow, yeah, whenever
Willem Dafoe shouts, "Dance,"

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:12.517
at you, it is a different,
like normally if someone says

00:03:12.517 --> 00:03:14.791
hey, do you wanna have a dance?

00:03:14.791 --> 00:03:16.159
It just wouldn't happen.

00:03:16.159 --> 00:03:18.927
♪ Dee dee dee dee dee dee
dee dee dee dee dee dee ♪

00:03:18.927 --> 00:03:20.017
- Dance!

00:03:20.017 --> 00:03:21.789
Dance, Winslow!

00:03:21.789 --> 00:03:22.882
Dance!

00:03:22.882 --> 00:03:25.132
(thudding)

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.137
♪ Come all you boys, do you want to hear ♪

00:03:29.137 --> 00:03:30.793
♪ How we got to the woods last year ♪

00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:33.560
- Yeah, that's one of my
favorite performances of yours,

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.410
I think Rob often surprised me,

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.570
this was one of these moments,

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:44.495
where he went further than I expected,

00:03:44.495 --> 00:03:45.880
but also slightly different

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:50.560
than what my preconceived
notions about the character.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:52.140
In the end of this clip,

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.600
when you seem like you're
speaking in tongues,

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:00.070
like everyone, the entire crew was shocked

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:02.770
